## Versioning

{% if ships_releases -%}
Releases follow SemVer: [auto-release](https://github.com/mbologna/auto-release)
tags `vX.Y.Z` from the Conventional Commit types (`feat` minor; `fix`,
`perf`, `revert` patch; a breaking change major). A weekly CI run (Monday
06:00 UTC) tags the next version when such a commit landed, or a
maintenance patch when dependency updates are waiting; a CVE fix releases
on the push that brings it. Only a tag builds and pushes the image, as
`X.Y.Z`, `X.Y` and `latest`, with the version in its
`org.opencontainers.image.version` label. `version` in `pyproject.toml` is a
placeholder and stays `0.0.0`. See the
[versioning standard](https://github.com/mbologna/.github/blob/main/VERSIONING.md).
{%- elif package and pypi_publish -%}
Releases follow SemVer: [auto-release](https://github.com/mbologna/auto-release)
tags `vX.Y.Z` from the Conventional Commit types (`feat` minor; `fix`,
`perf`, `revert` patch; a breaking change major). A weekly CI run (Monday
06:00 UTC) tags the next version when such a commit landed, or a
maintenance patch when dependency updates are waiting; a `fix(security)`
commit releases on the push that brings it. Each tag gets a GitHub Release
of the commit subjects, and `publish.yml` builds the tag with its version
and publishes it to [PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/{{ project_name }}/) with
trusted publishing. `version` in `pyproject.toml` is a placeholder and
stays `0.0.0`. See the
[versioning standard](https://github.com/mbologna/.github/blob/main/VERSIONING.md).
{%- elif package and changelog_releases -%}
Releases are the git tags `vX.Y.Z` and their {{ forge_name }} Releases, a changelog
of the commit subjects. They follow SemVer:
[auto-release](https://github.com/mbologna/auto-release) tags them from the
Conventional Commit types (`feat` minor; `fix`, `perf`, `revert` patch; a
breaking change major). A weekly CI run (Monday 06:00 UTC) tags the next
version when such a commit landed, or a maintenance patch when dependency
updates are waiting; a `fix(security)` commit releases on the push that
brings it. A tag builds nothing. `version` in `pyproject.toml` is a
placeholder and stays `0.0.0`. See the
[versioning standard](https://github.com/mbologna/.github/blob/main/VERSIONING.md).
{%- elif package -%}
Unversioned: there are no releases or tags. `version` in `pyproject.toml`
is a placeholder and stays `0.0.0`. See the
[versioning standard](https://github.com/mbologna/.github/blob/main/VERSIONING.md).
{%- elif changelog_releases -%}
Every push to main that changes the image publishes it as `latest` and
`sha-<commit>`{% if cloud_run != 'none' %} and deploys it, by digest, to the Cloud Run {{ cloud_run }}{% endif %}.
The `sha-*` images are the rollback window.

Releases are the git tags `vX.Y.Z` and their GitHub Releases, a changelog
of what main already {% if cloud_run != 'none' %}deployed{% else %}published{% endif %}. They follow SemVer:
[auto-release](https://github.com/mbologna/auto-release) tags them from the
Conventional Commit types (`feat` minor; `fix`, `perf`, `revert` patch; a
breaking change major). A weekly CI run (Monday 06:00 UTC) tags the next
version when such a commit landed, or a maintenance patch when dependency
updates are waiting; a CVE fix releases on the push that brings it. A tag
builds no image. `version` in `pyproject.toml` is a placeholder and stays
`0.0.0`. See the
[versioning standard](https://github.com/mbologna/.github/blob/main/VERSIONING.md).
{%- else -%}
Unversioned: there are no releases or tags. Every push to main that changes
the image publishes it as `latest` and `sha-<commit>`{% if cloud_run != 'none' %} and deploys it to the Cloud Run {{ cloud_run }}{% endif %}.
`version` in `pyproject.toml` is a placeholder and stays `0.0.0`. See the
[versioning standard](https://github.com/mbologna/.github/blob/main/VERSIONING.md).
{%- endif %}

## Development

```sh
uv run pytest                     # with the coverage gate from pyproject.toml
uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff format --check .
pre-commit install                # the same checks before each commit
{%- if not package %}
docker build -t {{ project_name }} .
{%- endif %}
```

Dependencies resolve only to releases at least 7 days old (`exclude-newer`
in `pyproject.toml`), and {% if package %}CI{% else %}the image{% endif %} installs exactly what `uv.lock` pins.
To take a CVE fix released less than 7 days ago, add the package to
`exclude-newer-package` as `<name> = false`, run `uv lock`, and remove the
entry once the release is a week old.
{%- if package and python_floor != '3.15' %}

The package supports Python {{ python_floor }} and newer (`requires-python` in
`pyproject.toml`). CI tests on Python 3.15 only, so keep syntax and
standard library features newer than {{ python_floor }} out of the code. Create the
virtual environment with that Python too (`uv venv --python 3.15`): uv may
otherwise pick an older one, on which some pre-commit hooks don't install.
{%- endif %}

The skeleton ({% if not package %}Dockerfile, {% endif %}CI, lint and test configuration) comes from
[python-app-template](https://github.com/mbologna/python-app-template);
Renovate proposes its updates as pull requests.
